Z||000000||Gomez||08-11-2001||11:25 AM||||Ok guys,<BR>This is 8ball, I am posting from work so my co-worker set u[p this account.<BR>I JUST bought my Fiero which I test drove for a good long hard run the other day. Well on my way to work I heard a LOUD pop and white smoke or steam I assume was spraying out of the vents in the deck lid. The engine must have overheated. The temp gauge seems to not work. What would the pop have been so I can make sure I can get the car home which is a 45 mile drive. I can't leave it here at work and The mechanic who Will help me with the car lives next door to me.<P>Also there was some water dripping out from under the car for a little bit not alot of water but some. It has since quit and the car is now harder to start but it will still start. Pleasde help me I have to get this car home so It can be fixed. and a tow truck will run me half as much as I paid for the car.<P>Thanks, <BR>Randy<BR>The depressed Fiero Owner<P>I knew I shoulda bought songman's, but I wanted a v6||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-11-2001||11:34 AM||||Well sounds like a coolant hose. Better get a tow truck to get it home.Or call mechanic to come to work and fix it there.Do not drive it in this condition .Oh you might want to look in engine compartment and have alook for yourself.This could show you something very obivous||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||08-11-2001||02:29 PM||||Check a couple of things: Coolant hoses, and the block-heater core plug. Follow the power cable to the unit. Mine did the same thing. the heater came out completely, resulting in total coolant pressure loss and overheating. DO NOT DRIVE THE THING!!!!!!!! You will kill the motor.||||reg||4
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||08-11-2001||03:17 PM||||Hey Randy!<BR>Check your coolant level before driving!!!<BR>I had something similar happen, the cap for the thermostat housing popped off...<BR>It was still in place, but one of the tabs popped off the neck of the housing...<BR>crash...<p>[This message has been edited by Fierowrecker (edited 08-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||8Ball||08-11-2001||10:52 PM||||Ok guys I am home and The Fiero is 3 hours away at a customers house. He came and towed it to his house so we can work on it tomorrow. This is what I have found out so far. Ok almost all the sensors in the car are either bypassed or gone. So I will be replaceing and rewireing all of them. Second, The last owner has also wired the fan straight to the ignition no temp switch. and third there is no overflow on the radiator the put a friggin bolt into the end of the overflow hose to seal it off so I will be buying that also tomorrow. IF I can find one, otherwise sometime next week I will have to go to the j/y to get one. He thinks I blew a plug or sumtin out of the back of the motor. So we are going to have to pull the motor tomorrow I guess.<BR>But he is sure I can have the car on the road and running right for under $150. Oh yea and it DOES NOT need an inner tie rod. It needs to be greased is all. so there is 150 saved.<P>Anyway Thanks a million and we will be checking all those as well of coarse. I am picking up a haynes manual on my way to tazwell tomorrow.<P><BR>I can't believe how they have butchered this poor Fiero. But on a happier note. The engine is very good, He says I got a good deal and there is only 91k miles on the car.<P><BR>Randy||||reg||1
